.SH NAME
niac-logs - View and stream simulation logs


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac logs [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
View and stream logs from a running NIAC simulation.

.PP
The logs command provides access to simulation logs including device activity,
protocol messages, and error injections. Logs can be filtered by level and
text pattern, and can be streamed in real-time with the tail subcommand.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for logs


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # View recent logs
  niac logs tail

  # Stream logs in real-time
  niac logs tail --follow

  # Filter by log level
  niac logs tail --level warn

  # Filter by text pattern
  niac logs tail --filter "device"

  # Output as JSON
  niac logs tail --json
.EE


